cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this master repository and, when materially used, the relevant component study."
title: "Cosmic Recurrence Framework: Dynamics, Predictive Equivalence, Observer Indistinguishability, Cosmic Coordinates, and Fate-Conditioned Cosmology"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sundy
    given-names: Scott A.
date-released: 2026-08-09
abstract: >-
  A reproducible master framework integrating exact and near recurrence diagnostics,
  protocol-family predictive quotients, exact finite observability certificates,
  hidden-state ambiguity, period and phase navigation, observer-indistinguishability,
  a model-conditional cosmic coordinate, and fate-conditioned partial identification
  of cosmological recurrence. Finite benchmark recurrence is not used as cosmological
  evidence, and current inputs do not identify a physical cosmic recurrence phase or
  a unique model-independent recurrence probability.
keywords:
  - recurrence dynamics
  - predictive equivalence
  - predictive quotient
  - observer indistinguishability
  - hidden-state ambiguity
  - phase navigation
  - cosmic coordinate
  - cosmological recurrence
  - de Sitter
  - partial identification
  - computational physics
